		summary = '"**The Raven**" is a narrative poem by American writer [[Edgar Allan Poe]]. First published in January 1845, the poem is often noted for its musicality, stylized language and supernatural atmosphere. Sitting on a bust of [[Athena|Pallas]], the raven seems to antagonize the protagonist further with its repetition of the word. The poem makes use of [[Folklore|folk]], mythological, religious, and [[Classical antiquity|classical]] references.',
